    {
      "id": "LFT-03",
      "title": "Stable-range split parameter",
      "statement": "For the paired types in a fixed row, under the Bernstein–Zelevinsky finiteness and Bernstein irreducibility inputs, reading laws, row unitarisability, local pairing and goodness of the target, the split-place target parameter is the direct sum of the row parameter and the extra segment, with the final twist. The ranks satisfy r=k+m−1, nV=r+t and r+5≤t. The extra segment consists of t twists of μ with exponents (t−1)/2−h for 0≤h<t, and the full sum is twisted by η⁻¹.",
